WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.270
- We're back and last year,

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:04.290
I met an extraordinary
woman giving help and hope

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:05.890
to countless unhoused men and women,

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:07.620
living here in Los Angeles.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:09.450
Not only does she personally make meals

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:11.280
to feed people along Skid Row,

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:13.770
she's rallied an army of
volunteers to help out.

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:16.220
And that's just one
piece of what she does.

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:18.010
Let's look back at my time with Jackie,

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:19.960
also known as the Brown Bag Lady.

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:20.793
(swooshing)

00:00:20.793 --> 00:00:23.820
- I'm proud to say that
everything we do is from scratch

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:26.490
and we just make meals every week.

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:29.700
And it just, we have not missed a Sunday

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.750
and that's just amazing to me.

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:35.080
We give out free haircuts,
we give out clothes,

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:36.450
gently used shoes.

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:38.290
And so, it's just a group of us.

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:40.740
We literally get together every weekend,

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:45.160
we go through everything, we
put it by size, male, female.

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:49.430
And in addition to the
meal, we give you clothes,

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:52.290
sanitary items for the ladies.

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:54.857
And so, that's why we
came up with the logo,

00:00:54.857 --> 00:00:56.680
"Feeding the body, nourishing the soul".

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:58.129
It's not just a meal.

00:00:58.129 --> 00:00:59.280
(audience applauds)

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:00.113
- I love that.

00:01:00.113 --> 00:01:01.850
Jackie's compassionate work,

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:04.380
landed her a hefty, $50,000,

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:06.650
overachievers grant from Pilot pen,

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:08.890
which has only helped her do even more.

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:11.050
We have her with us right now.

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:12.931
It's great to finally meet you in person.

00:01:12.931 --> 00:01:13.901
(audience applauds)
- Nice to meet you.

00:01:13.901 --> 00:01:15.280
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- Thank you for having me.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:16.950
- [Kelly] Oh, my God, I'm
so excited you're here.

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:19.000
And you must've been
thrilled to get the grant.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.530
- Oh my gosh, my sister's
friend nominated me.

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:23.420
I was standing in the reception area

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:25.100
of the law office, where I work

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:27.247
and the guy on the other
end of the phone says,

00:01:27.247 --> 00:01:30.560
"Jacqueline Norvell, you
are the grand prize winner

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:34.737
of the Pilot pen, G2
overachiever, $50,000 grant".

00:01:34.737 --> 00:01:35.570
(Jackie gasps)

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:36.600
Oh, it was so exciting.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:38.670
I still get chills when I think about it.

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:42.640
I mean, the wonderful
Pilot pen team picked me up

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:46.374
and presented me with
a cheque for $50,000.

00:01:46.374 --> 00:01:47.207
- [Kelly] That's amazing.

00:01:47.207 --> 00:01:48.165
(audience applauds)

00:01:48.165 --> 00:01:49.336
- It was awesome.

00:01:49.336 --> 00:01:50.976
(audience applauds)

00:01:50.976 --> 00:01:52.230
- [Kelly] What'd you end up
getting to do with the money?

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:55.310
- Oh my goodness, so,
we were doing everything

00:01:55.310 --> 00:01:58.250
out of my 2005, Nissan, Pathfinder.

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:00.080
So we were able to buy a van.

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:00.913
- [Kelly] Oh, good.

00:02:00.913 --> 00:02:01.840
- And we bought a van

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:05.360
and we have men's clothes on one side

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:07.640
and women's clothes on the other side,

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:12.640
we have hygiene products,
full toiletries for the men,

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:15.090
we have shoes, we have socks.

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:18.330
We just totally load the van up.

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:20.170
And then it was also great,

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:23.990
because every year we take backpacks

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:27.730
to an underserved school and we fill them.

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:29.040
It's not just a backpack.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:32.850
We get together and we fill
it with school supplies.

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:34.670
- Because that's expensive and
families can't afford that.

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:36.240
- They can't, they cannot.

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.900
And it's just been, you know, phenomenal.

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:40.440
And we buy the backpacks,

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:42.270
it's not like I'm point and click.

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:45.170
I literally go to a warehouse,

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:47.650
because what a pre-k child wants,

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:49.020
a fifth grader does not want.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:52.650
So, they're tailored to the,
you know, to each grade and...

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:53.490
- [Kelly] You're investing in them.

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:54.610
- Yes, yes.

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:56.130
- Yeah and people do better with that.

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:57.920
Kids that know that people care

00:02:57.920 --> 00:02:59.770
and give them something
like that, they work harder.

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:00.603
- [Jackie] Yes.

00:03:00.603 --> 00:03:01.510
- And they, they want to pay it forward

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:03.950
and invest in others as well,
it's a great domino effect.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:04.783
- It is.

00:03:04.783 --> 00:03:07.930
- So, and now you've taken
on a new, ambitious project.

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:08.910
So what's this?

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:10.110
- Oh my gosh.

00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:14.020
Okay so, in dealing and
talking and chatting,

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:16.420
because you know, the
homeless become your friend,

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:19.130
you see them every weekend,
you talk with them,

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:20.930
you know their background.

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:24.880
I realize that a lot were
in the foster care system

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:27.450
and had been separated from
their brother and sister.

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:28.440
I just assumed,

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:30.810
you have a brother and
sister, you go together.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:34.620
No, the sister could go,
say in San Bernardino

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:36.720
and the brother is, you
know, in Orange County

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:40.060
and they get to see each other
once a month, for one hour.

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:42.360
And then it starts the downward spiral.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:43.193
- Oh wow.

00:03:43.193 --> 00:03:45.000
- [Jackie] So, what we
are committed to doing,

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.170
and we are going to do it.

00:03:47.170 --> 00:03:48.770
We are going to...

00:03:50.084 --> 00:03:50.917
I'm sorry.

00:03:50.917 --> 00:03:51.760
- [Kelly] No, oh my gosh.

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:53.200
It's an amazing thing that you're doing

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:54.440
and it should touch you.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:58.610
- We are going to reunite
siblings that have been separated.

00:03:58.610 --> 00:03:59.443
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:59.443 --> 00:04:00.810
- By the system.

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:03.070
And no matter where they are,
no matter where they're at,

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:04.220
we're gonna bring them together

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:07.558
for one week of sleep away
camp and I'm so excited.

00:04:07.558 --> 00:04:08.908
- [Kelly] Oh, my God.
(audience applauds)

00:04:08.908 --> 00:04:10.417
Oh my gosh.

00:04:10.417 --> 00:04:11.250
- Yes.

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:12.083
- Here, here, here, here.

00:04:12.083 --> 00:04:13.092
- I'm so excited.

00:04:13.092 --> 00:04:15.321
(audience applauds)

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:16.900
- Well all right, well, good news,

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:18.810
our season long partner, Pilot pen

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:21.760
is looking for the next $100,000,

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:23.100
G2 overachievers grant winner.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:26.130
And they want to recognize
one, exceptional individual,

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:29.180
who goes above and beyond
their everyday responsibilities

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:31.800
to improve the lives of
others, like you have.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:35.040
And this $100,000 grant will
greatly expand their reach

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:38.020
to communities in need,
but that's not all,

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:40.290
Pilot also wants to celebrate exceptional,

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:42.892
young scholars with a $15,000,

00:04:42.892 --> 00:04:45.590
G2 overachievers student grant,

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:47.810
which is... That creates
so much opportunity,

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:49.230
which is a beautiful thing.

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:53.210
This will recognize young
people, 13 to 19 years old,

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:54.560
who are excelling in their studies

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.600
and making a real
difference in other's lives

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:58.410
outside the classroom.

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:01.410
If you know, a remarkable
person going above and beyond

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:02.890
to improve their community,

00:05:02.890 --> 00:05:05.960
please submit a handwritten
nomination, right now.

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:07.030
Let's do it.

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:08.670
The deadline for the $100,000,

00:05:08.670 --> 00:05:12.550
G2 overachievers grant
is January 15th, 2022.

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:15.080
And the deadline for the
$15,000, student grant

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:17.820
is right around the corner,
November 15th, 2021.

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:19.130
So, get on it.

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:22.900
Go to G2overachievers.com to learn more.

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:24.200
Thank you so much.
(audience applauds)

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:25.033
- [Jackie] Absolutely.

00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:26.840
- And I want us to keep in contact,

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:28.298
helping out with what you're doing.

00:05:28.298 --> 00:05:29.131
- For sure.

00:05:29.131 --> 00:05:29.964
- [Kelly] It's such a cool thing.

00:05:29.964 --> 00:05:30.797
- Thank you, thank you.

00:05:30.797 --> 00:05:31.630
- [Kelly] And it's important,

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:32.491
especially for those foster kids.

00:05:32.491 --> 00:05:33.324
- Thank you for shining light.

00:05:33.324 --> 00:05:35.750
I really appreciate you shining
light on our non-profit.

